# Pending-before-production reminder

## When to remind

At the **start of every new user request** (after a break, new chat, or a fresh “do X” ask), **before** starting the requested work:

1. Read `docs/PENDING_BEFORE_PRODUCTION.md`.
2. Open a short **Pending before production** block (3–8 bullets max) listing still-open **Must clear** items.
3. Note **Parked** items only if the user’s ask would collide with them (do not nag parked work otherwise).
4. Then proceed with what the user asked — unless they explicitly say to clear pending items first.

## When to skip the reminder

- User says “skip pending reminder” / “no status” for this turn.
- Pure follow-up in the same continuous turn (same task, same session, no context loss).
- User is already working on an item from that list.

## Keeping the list honest

- When an item is verified done, update `docs/PENDING_BEFORE_PRODUCTION.md` in the same change set (or immediately after).
- When new production blockers appear, add them there — do not rely on chat memory alone.
- Do not invent urgency; keep wording factual and short.
